# --- harness ---
# Run dirs are ephemeral scratch. They MUST be ignored: a dirty tree halts a team run
# with BLOCKED, so without this the harness's own artifacts deadlock the next run.
# Everything else under .harness/ is committed on purpose — BRIEF, PLAN, STATE,
# notes, logs, expertise and features/*/feature.json are the record of what shipped,
# and reviewers auditing the PR diff need to see plan and state changes.
.harness/features/*/runs/**
# The metrics dashboard's installed dependency tree and Vite cache (FEAT-53). An installed
# dependency tree dirties the working tree, and a dirty tree halts the next team run — the
# same reason the run-dir rule above exists. dist/ is NOT ignored: the built bundle is
# committed on purpose (D-04).
.claude/skills/harness/bin/dashboard/client/node_modules/
.claude/skills/harness/bin/dashboard/client/.vite/
# Deliberately NOT ignored (D-22): .harness/metrics/instrumented_at and each feature's
# touchpoints.jsonl are committed records. An ignore rule over the epoch would let a second
# clone write a later instant, and a feature starting after that fabricated epoch would
# report a measured zero — exactly what D-21 exists to prevent. No rule for either path;
# this comment is the whole of it.
# The one-session PyYAML bootstrap marker (DEC-171). Written by the write hooks
# when PyYAML is missing, so the FIRST session can still recover; untracked, it would
# dirty the tree and deadlock the next run on the very rule above.
.harness/.pyyaml-bootstrap
__pycache__/
*.pyc
.claude/settings.json.harness-bak
.claude/settings.local.json
.claude/worktrees/
.DS_Store
# --- end harness ---
